&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="data"&gt;Data&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="data"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#data" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Data arguments take &lt;code&gt;[]float64&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[]float32&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[]int&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[]int32&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[]int64&lt;/code&gt;,
a scalar, or a &lt;code&gt;*ndarray.Array&lt;/code&gt; of any of &lt;a href="https://github.com/go-ndarray/ndarray" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;go-ndarray&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s
dtypes. A type that cannot be plotted, or &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; of different lengths,
&lt;strong&gt;panics&lt;/strong&gt;: both are programming errors, as an index out of range is. See
&lt;a href="https://go-plot.github.io/docs/0.1/api/#data-is-any"&gt;the API&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="in-a-notebook"&gt;In a notebook&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="in-a-notebook"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#in-a-notebook" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;fig.Display()&lt;/code&gt; returns the figure in every format a notebook front end may
show, keyed by MIME type: &lt;code&gt;image/svg+xml&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;image/png&lt;/code&gt;. It is the display
contract of the &lt;a href="https://github.com/go-notebook/notebook" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;go-notebook&lt;/a&gt; kernel,
so a cell whose last expression is a figure shows it; it is the notebook&amp;rsquo;s
&lt;code&gt;plt.show()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
